Let's analyze your situation:

1) No reflection, no MR, no AOLS - any chameleon could insta-kill you
in a single turn.
2) You have a good ranged attack.
3) You know a few powerful spells, but you are wearing mithril, which
limits your spellcasting potential. You also have only 72 PW.
4) You have charged wands of fire, lightning, digging and teleportation
in your main inventory, which is GOOD; you can engrave a permanent
Elbereth in a single turn, or escape in 3 different ways.
5) You have an unrecharged magic marker with only 9 charges remaining.
6) You have 2 wands of polymorph with 7 charges remaining.
7) You have useful rings of invisibility, slow digest, and free action.

Suggestions:
1) Climb out of the deep dungeon. A chameleon instakill would SUCK
2) Dump the mithril immediately for studded leather. You NEED to be
able to cast "charm monster" and "stone-to-flesh" with 0% fail.
3) On your way up, cast "detect treasure" on every level, and carefully
open all the chests (#untrap and drop wands/rings before opening).
There could be a [CoMR somewhere.
4) You are neutral, you have a =RoSD, and you can cast "create
monster".  You can sacrifice until you get Magicbane, unless Magicbane
already exists somewhere.  This is easier if you use pudding farming,
but with a little patience you can definitely get MR this way. This is
safest if you have a co-aligned temple, but you can also do this
without much risk using a single burned Elbereth. You can also sac for
spellbooks and protection.
5) For reflection, you can create monsters on the Oracle level until
you get a baby silver dragon, which you should tame. Let it grow into
an adult, then wound it with your arrows until it is badly hurt, then
let it die in battle. If it doesn't leave scales try again.
6) You could polypile spellbooks, scrolls, potions, unicorn horns,
elvin cloaks/boots, rings (uncurse them first), mundane armor, and
pets. 7 charges of polymorph would give you a good chance of getting a
[SoR or [COMR.  You could also get magic markers or scrolls of
charging.
7) Once you have a magic marker with enough charges you can try writing
"genocide" without knowing it. If your luck is maxxed, you have a fair
chance even though you aren't a wizard.
8) Ludios - you could clear it (of soldiers) without risk using a pet
purple worm. Is there a black dragon there? If so, you can use an
burned Elbereth in the right place to let it into the second room
without it being able to breathe at you. You could tame it, or put it
to sleep and slay it. Your biggest risk is if someone on the level has
a wand of death. A pet purple worm could avoid that risk.
9) Consider poisoning your arrows. Potions of sickness are easy to make
with alchemy. Poisoned arrows do much more damage on average.
10) Leave some of your junk in a stash. There is no reason to be
carrying around so many oil lamps.

